      "message": "Once the plugin is unloaded, `newLock()` throws `IllegalStateException`. `tryAcquireRaw()` catches it as a `RuntimeException`, logs it at SEVERE, and the batching lock goes on retrying with backoff until `h2LockTimeout` runs out. So each call to `getConnection()` blocks for the whole timeout (30 s by default) and logs a SEVERE stack trace up to every 500 ms. That covers reads too: `findReviewed` and the reviewed-files lookup behind the diff and file views, not only writes as the docs say. On a busy primary this ties up request threads after a plain plugin uninstall. Since this state is permanent until the plugin is reinstalled, could `getConnection()` fail fast before entering the batching lock? For example:\n```java\n@Override\npublic Connection getConnection() throws SQLException {\n  if (lockManager.get() instanceof DefaultLockManager) {\n    throw new SQLException(\"...no plugin-provided LockManager bound...\");\n  }\n  return super.getConnection();\n}\n```\nThe docs sentence about writes failing should then also mention reads.",
